  "dataCard": {},
  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/apistogramma-atahualpa-4/",
      "html": "<p>Before its scientific description this beautiful species of dwarf cichlid from Peru was known in the hobby as the \"Sunset-Apistogramma\". The body coloration of a female during brood care reminds one of a sunset.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/apistogramma-atahualpa-4/",
      "html": "<p>Currently beautiful wild-collected specimens of A. atahualpa are being obtained.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/apistogramma-atahualpa-4/",
      "html": "<p>The scientific name, atahualpa, refers to the last great ruler of the Inka empire, Atahualpa. He was captured by the Spaniard Pizarro in 1532 and executed in 1533; this was the sunset of the Inka empire.</p>"
    }
  ],
